Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Cara-Delevingne.md` (Type 4 draft, ~3,300 body words) against the entity-gap packet and the research file, and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom.

**The two biggest flags:**

1. **Her queerness is missing from the article entirely** — and it was cut out of the load-bearing pull-quote. Her actual line is *"I knew I was a little queer kid running around. I didn't feel like I belonged in my body, in my family, in any of it."* The draft uses only the second sentence, so the not-belonging quote loses the specific thing it was about. Meanwhile the strongest unused item in the research file is on the same subject: *"Harvey Weinstein called me and was like, 'You can't be gay.'"* That is an industry paying her to perform unfiltered honesty while instructing her to hide the real thing — which is the billboard thesis. (Needs strict attribution as her own on-record account.)

2. **The final act has no skeptic in it.** The Rabbit Hole names the 4w3 shadow as "performing authenticity rather than embodying it," then the piece never asks whether *Not Normal* — sold on rawness, launched alongside a Rag & Bone campaign following the tour — is subject to the same charge. All critic pressure lands in section 5 and is fully rebutted before the album section starts, so the draft resolves into a clean redemption arc.

Also worth knowing before the next pass: Minke appears zero times despite the piece quoting "the opposite of addiction is connection"; *Only Murders in the Building* and Cabaret/Sally Bowles are both absent, so the career-collecting section concedes "she has no talents" without the two credits that rebut it; and two of the five quotes in the testimony ledger (Gomez, Besson) never reach the body. There's roughly 1,200 words of headroom under the 4,500 lint ceiling, so the additions fit.
